r":false,"num_turns":20,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"`work/weights.npz`, `work/NOTES.md` and `work/predictions.json` are in place. W2, b2, W3 and b3 are byte-identical to the source network's. Nothing was fitted and no simulator was run.\n\n**Mapping:** I set W1 = W1_L2 @ M and kept b1 = b1_L2. M is a fixed 46×54 matrix that turns an L2W observation into a \"virtual L2\" observation, matching lanes by which upstream lane feeds them:\n- L2's right+straight lane gets the mean of L2W's E0 and E1, which both have their own upstream lane.\n- L2's straight lane beside the left pocket gets L2W's E2; the left pocket gets E3.\n- Upstream: E0u/E1u are averaged, and E2u (straight+left) maps on at full weight.\n- I used per-lane means, not sums, because L2W's per-lane EW through load (~245 veh/h) is close to L2's (~262).\n- N/S stop-line lanes are shorter on L2W (19.2 m vs 22.4 m), so I scaled those inputs by 0.937.\n\n**Checks:**\n- With no N/S scaling, the mapping reproduces the source logits exactly (error 1.8e-15).\n- Agreement with the source network's decisions is 95.6% with the N/S scaling.\n- The other mapping variants agree on about 95% of states; summing lanes changes 17%.\n- Synthetic scenarios behave sensibly, with no NS starvation.\n\n**Trainability:** median max_prob 0.992 (source 0.982), share above 0.99 0.52, median logit gap 4.97, sat_l1 0.0003, sat_l2 0.097, no dead units. W1 is no larger than the source's.\n\n**Predicted test TTS (veh-h):** low 45.5, nominal 59.5, high 76.5. These are rough estimates scaled from the source's 44.5 on L2 and the dev references.","ttft_ms":1290,"type":"result","duration_ms":407894,"uuid":"1b692eb6-246b-4717-9ed9-45b27e8f634b","ttft_stream_ms":1135,"time_to_request_ms":197,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":12,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":10,"input_attachments":24,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":40,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":8,"init_frame